                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-28",
                                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                                    "numinlets": 2,
                                    "numoutlets": 1,
                                    "outlettype": [ "signal" ],
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 365.0, 37.0, 23.0 ],
                                    "rnbo_classname": "-~",
                                    "rnbo_serial": 1,
                                    "rnbo_uniqueid": "-~_obj-28",
                                    "text": "-~ 20"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-27",
                                    "linecount": 24,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 689.0, 264.0, 280.0, 352.0 ],
                                    "text": "4. Amp envelope used to scale filter cutoff frequency, as determined by filter_env parameter. If filter_env >= 0, filter envelope modulation is positive from the starting cutoff frequency, so the max range of envelope modulation is determined by the max cutoff frequency of the filter minus the current cutoff frequency value as determined by the cutoff parameter (!-~ 12500). If filter_env < 0, filter envelope modulation is negative from the starting cutoff frequency, so the max range of envelope modulation is determined by the current cutoff frequency minus the min cutoff frequency of the filter (-~ 20). The amplitude envelope is first scaled by the filter_env param, with negative filter_env values inverting the envelope, before subsequently being scaled by the max filter envelope range. The scaled amplitude envelope is then summed with the current cutoff frequency, as determined by the cutoff parameter, at 4a. feedback~ imparts a single sample vector delay into the signal path, which is necessary for feeding the scaled amplitude envelope signal back into the filter cutoff frequency due to the fact that the filter precedes the amplitude envelope in the signal path. "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 284.0, 207.0, 40.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "4a."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                    "id": "obj-23",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 344.0, 398.0, 31.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "4."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-22",
                                    "linecount": 2,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 689.0, 227.0, 280.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "3. Note velocity converted to gate (note on = 1, note off = 0) in order to trigger amplitude envelope."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                    "id": "obj-21",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 344.0, 283.0, 31.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "3."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                    "id": "obj-20",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 154.0, 359.0, 31.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "2."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                    "id": "obj-19",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 206.0, 54.0, 31.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "1."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-13",
                                    "linecount": 10,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 689.0, 75.0, 280.0, 150.0 ],
                                    "text": "2. Note on velocity value (0–1) latched on note onset by impulse trigger derived from increase in velocity value from preceding note off value of 0 when a new note is triggered. This increase in velocity is detected by delta~ and converted to an impulse trigger by >~. The latched note on velocity value (0–1) is then used to scale the outgoing signal level after its amplitude has been enveloped by sbb.env.analog, thus imparting MIDI velocity control over the output of the synth."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-11",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 689.0, 23.0, 280.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "1. Incoming MIDI note pitch converted to frequency signal and MIDI note velocity scaled to 0–1 range and also converted to a signal."
                                }
                            },
